# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in values from your Supabase project
# (Project Settings -> API in the Supabase dashboard).

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# --- Optional: only needed for automatic (scheduled) calendar sync. ---
# Without these, iCal feeds still work fine via the "Sync now" / "Sync all
# feeds" buttons on the Properties page -- just not on a schedule. See
# webapp/README.md "Automatic sync" for setting up a free external
# scheduler (e.g. cron-job.org) to call /api/cron/sync-ical periodically.
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY bypasses Row Level Security. Keep it out of
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* (never sent to the browser), out of the repo, and only set
# it where the cron route actually runs (e.g. Vercel project env vars).
# From Project Settings -> API Keys -> the secret/service-role key.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
#
# A random secret you generate yourself (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`).
# Whatever calls /api/cron/sync-ical on a schedule must send it as an
# `Authorization: Bearer <value>` header -- this is how the route checks
# the request is really your own scheduled job and not the public internet.
# CRON_SECRET=

# --- Optional: only needed for push notifications. ---
# Without these, the app still works fine, and the "Enable notifications"
# button just won't appear -- see webapp/README.md "Mobile app access +
# push notifications" for how to generate your own pair with
# `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY must match VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY exactly (the
# public half is sent to the browser to subscribe; the server needs the
# same value again alongside the private key to sign outgoing pushes).
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY must be kept out of the repo and out of NEXT_PUBLIC_*.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.com

# --- Optional: only needed for SMS notifications. ---
# Without these, the app still works fine, and the "Also text me
# booking/job alerts" checkbox on the Profile page just won't do anything
# -- see webapp/README.md "SMS notifications" for how to get a Twilio
# account and an Australian phone number to send from.
#
# From your Twilio Console dashboard (console.twilio.com).
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=AC...
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=...
#
# The Twilio phone number you send texts from, in E.164 format
# (Phone Numbers -> Manage -> Active Numbers). Buying an Australian
# number requires Twilio to verify your business first (a quick online
# form) -- budget a day or two before your first text can go out.
# TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=+614xxxxxxxx

# --- Optional: only needed for Stripe-backed features (cleaner ID
# verification via Stripe Identity, cleaner payouts via Stripe Connect,
# subscription billing via Stripe Billing). Without these, the app works
# exactly the same and those features simply don't appear.
#
# From your Stripe dashboard -> Developers -> API keys. Use the *test
# mode* keys while building; switch to live keys only once you're ready
# to take real payments. Keep STRIPE_SECRET_KEY out of the repo and out
# of NEXT_PUBLIC_* -- it's a server-only secret.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
#
# From Developers -> Webhooks -> your endpoint -> Signing secret, once
# you've added https://your-app.vercel.app/api/webhooks/stripe as an
# endpoint listening for the events each feature needs (see README).
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
#
# The Price id for the single $2/property/month subscription Price
# (Product catalog -> your product -> the Price's id, starts "price_").
# Test mode and live mode each have their own id -- use whichever matches
# the STRIPE_SECRET_KEY above. See src/lib/billing.ts.
# STRIPE_PRICE_PER_PROPERTY=price_...

# --- Optional: only needed for the checklist photo reviewer. ---
# Without this, the app still works fine -- a cleaner's photos just don't
# get an automated AI review. See webapp/docs/PHOTO_REVIEWER.md for what
# it does and how it fails open.
#
# From console.anthropic.com -> API Keys. Each completed booking's photos
# cost roughly a cent to review, so keep this out of the repo like any
# other secret key.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#
# Optional: override the model used for photo reviews (defaults to the
# cheapest current Claude vision model). Only worth setting if you want a
# more capable model reviewing photos, at higher cost per booking.
# ANTHROPIC_PHOTO_REVIEW_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
